# Files Fern must not modify or delete when regenerating this repo.
#
# Fern owns the SDK source and prunes anything it did not generate — it reads this file
# from the pull request's base branch, so an entry only protects a file once it is on
# main. This file has to land before Fern's first PR merges.
#
# publish-main.yml is hand-written. There is no Swift package registry: SwiftPM resolves
# this git repository and its tags directly, so the tag *is* the release. The workflow
# tags main when a merge lands a Sources/Version.swift that the remote has no tag for.
#
# ci.yml is hand-written too, for the opposite reason to whopsdk-ruby's. fern-swift-sdk
# 0.36.0 emits no .github directory at all — no ci.yml, no publish job — so nothing
# compiles this tree, nothing runs its 411 generated tests and nothing notices when a
# regeneration reverts one of the patches below. Verified against the generated tree on
# 2026-08-21; if a future generator version starts emitting a ci.yml, reconcile the two
# rather than dropping this one.
#
# The three files under Sources/Core are GENERATED files carrying hand-written patches, so
# every entry here freezes that file at fern-swift-sdk 0.36.0. That cost is bounded: all
# three are template/asIs files whose only spec-derived content is the SDK's own error-enum
# name and the retry status list, so they do not drift as the API grows — unlike, say,
# Sources/Whop.swift, which gains a property per resource and is why the Api-Version-Date
# default lives in HTTPClient rather than in the constructor where Fern puts it. Each patch
# is asserted by name in ci.yml's hand-written-guards job, so a regeneration that reverts
# one fails there instead of on a caller's machine. Delete an entry and its patch when the
# generator fixes the defect upstream.
#
#   - Serde.swift — sets `outputFormatting = [.sortedKeys]` on the request encoder.
#     Foundation promises no key order for a keyed container, so without it one request
#     value encodes to different bytes on different calls. Whop fingerprints
#     Idempotency-Key over the request body, so the API's double-charge protection is
#     unreachable from Swift until this is set. `outputFormatting` appears nowhere in
#     fern-swift-sdk 0.36.0's bundle, so no generator config can produce it.
#
#   - KeyedDecodingContainer+Nullable.swift — adds an absent-tolerant `decode` overload for
#     `Nullable<T>`. Generated models read every nullable response field with
#     `container.decode`, which throws `keyNotFound` on a missing key, so a pinned older
#     Api-Version-Date or any legitimately downgraded payload fails the WHOLE response.
#     The overload is more specialized than the stdlib's generic `decode`, so it wins
#     overload resolution at 954 generated call sites without any of them changing. The
#     `nullableAsOptional: true` generator config reaches the same outcome by turning every
#     `Nullable<T>` into `T?`, but it also erases the null-vs-omitted distinction on request
#     bodies, which a PATCH surface needs.
#
#   - HTTPClient.swift — four fixes, all in the one file that already owns the wire:
#       * sends the Api-Version-Date the SDK was generated against. Fern's IR carries the
#         default (`clientDefault`, from `x-fern-default`) and fern-swift-sdk parses it and
#         never reads it, hardcoding `nil` instead, so an unpinned Swift caller is served
#         the API's OLDEST contract and cannot read products at all.
#       * sends User-Agent and the X-Fern-SDK-* identity headers. The generator emits none,
#         so `Sources/Version.swift` was dead code and a Swift caller was indistinguishable
#         in Whop's access logs from any other program on the platform.
#       * encodes array query parameters as repeated bare keys. `QueryParameter.toString()`
#         renders `.stringArray` as one comma-joined value, which is lossy for any id that
#         can contain a comma.
#       * reads `RequestOptions.additionalBodyParameters`, which is public and documented
#         and which `buildRequestBody` accepted and ignored; and surfaces cancellation as
#         `WhopSDKError` at every retry setting rather than a bare `CancellationError` on
#         all but the last attempt.
#
# LICENSE is deliberately NOT listed. Fern writes it from `license: Apache-2.0` in the
# swift-release github block of whop-monorepo's sdks/fern/generators.yml, the same way
# whopsdk-ruby and whopsdk-python get theirs — neither of which .fernignores it. The file
# is committed here so the repository has one before the next regeneration lands.
.github/workflows/ci.yml
.github/workflows/publish-main.yml
Sources/Core/Networking/HTTPClient.swift
Sources/Core/Serde/KeyedDecodingContainer+Nullable.swift
Sources/Core/Serde/Serde.swift
